      "cooked": "<p>I believe I have stumbled across something beautiful and would like to confirm that I have played it correctly.</p>\n<p>The Chairman is in play, and has been flipped.  Writhe is in play, and has his Caliginous Form card active.  Writhe inflicts damage on the Chairman.  The Chairman retaliates for 3 HP of damage.  Caliginous Form reduces that to 1 HP and redirects it to the Chairman, who currently the highest-HP villain.  Then, because he has been damaged by a target that so happens to be himself, he retaliates and inflicts another 3 HP of damage on himself.</p>\n<p>Does that sound right?</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:41:24.764Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
