      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pydro/{size}/1844_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-05-26T14:09:29.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ronway\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/48/1856_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ronway:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>McBehrer wrote:</b><br><blockquote>No, that sounds right to me. It's the first time each target hits him, just like backlash field, flame barrier, and combat stance.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div><blockquote>\nThe first time The Chairman is dealt damage each turn, deal the source of the damage x melee damage.\n</blockquote><blockquote>\nThe first time Ra is dealt damage by a target each turn, Ra deals tha target 2 fire damage.\n</blockquote>\nArgent Adept allows Ra to use a power, he burns The Chairman for some fire damage. The Chairman hits Ra back since it is the first time The Chairman was dealt damage. Now that Ra was dealt damage for the first time this turn by a target, Ra deals The Chairman 2 fire damage.Argent Adept then allows Haka to play Rampage. It deals The Chairman 5 melee damage. This is not the first time The Chairman has been dealt damage, thus no damage dealt back to Haka. Haka then hits heroes for 2 damage, which includes Ra. This is the first time Ra has been dealt damage by the target, Haka now takes 2 fire damage.Different triggers.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Wow, I never thought the Cursed Acolyte would come to my rescue. This is strange. What am I supposed to do or feel.</p>",
